  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Monday)\nIssued at 1200 AM CDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\nOur seemingly endless stretch of abnormal heat furthermore has no \nend in sight, as model trends continue to show upper level ridging \ndominating the synoptic pattern. Both deterministic and ensemble \ndatasets depict high pressure being nudged eastward over the \nsoutheast CONUS through the week, and then morphing back on top of \nthe Plains this weekend as persistent troughing settles atop the \nPacific northwest. Moisture transport to the Panhandles will be \nscarce, while high temperatures steadily remain in the 90 to 105 \nrange each day. If there are any better rain chances, models suggest \nThursday could see slightly improved potential as the jet stream \nsags closer to the Panhandles. However, this still only supports \nmeager 10-20% POPs to mainly far northwestern portions of the \nforecast area. \n\nHarrel",
